<title>GERMANY: German building industry sees 98 investment flat.</title>
<headline>German building industry sees 98 investment flat.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A German construction industry group said on Wednesday that it expected building investment to stagnate in 1998.</p>
<p>Fritz Eichbauer, president of the Central Association of German Construction Firms (ZDB) said at a news conference the group expected investment growth in west Germany of one percent next year. In eastern Germany, construction investment was expected to fall three percent.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
